[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138725,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Yolk sac tumour (YST) is a malignant germ cell neoplasm with variable histological patterns reflecting stages in the phylogenetic development of extraembryonic membranes such as the allantois and the yolk sac.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138726,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9071/3 Yolk sac tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138727,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2D04 &amp; XH09W7 Malignant neoplasm of orbit &amp; Yolk sac tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138728,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> endodermal sinus tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138729,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138730,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>YST occurs in the orbit, most often in the extraconal space, with possible extension into the nasopharynx, paranasal sinuses, or cranium {26481249}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138731,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital YST usually presents in early childhood with an average presentation age of 27&nbsp;months {26481249;18219360;32594074;35258404}. One orbital YST arose at age 14&nbsp;years {22096462}, but all others arose at &le;&nbsp;4&nbsp;years of age. The M:F&nbsp;ratio is 1:1.6 (7&nbsp;male patients vs 11&nbsp;female patients). Common clinical features include progressive proptosis, ptosis, ophthalmoplegia, vision loss, relative afferent pupillary defect, exposure keratopathy, and inflammatory symptoms and signs {26481249}. Orbital YST may be well delineated or infiltrative on CT or MRI {26481249}. Serum AFP was elevated in the cases where it was measured {12426694;18030121;35258404;32594074}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138732,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital YST is rare, with only 19&nbsp;reported cases {26481249;18219360;32594074;35258404}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138733,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138734,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital YST is postulated to arise from ectopic extraembryonic germ cells or defective embryogenesis {26481249;8066543}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138735,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not available</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138736,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Orbital YSTs feature a meshwork of spaces lined by flat to cuboidal epithelium with marked cellular anaplasia and conspicuous mitoses {6677841}. There may be a microcystic, macrocystic, reticular, alveolar-glandular, or myxomatous pattern {26481249}. Schiller&ndash;Duval bodies (fibrovascular cores covered by a layer of embryonic epithelium) may be present or absent {26481249}. The stroma and tumour cells contain hyaline globules that are PAS-positive and diastase resistant {6677841;26481249}. There is strong cytoplasmic staining for AFP, CAM5.2 {26481249}, and glypican-3 (GPC3) {32594074}, and nuclear expression of SALL4 {32594074}, similarly to other extragonadal YSTs {19574883}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138737,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant&nbsp;/ not described for orbital YSTs</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138738,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138739,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> primitive germ cell tumour exhibiting stages in the phylogenetic development of extraembryonic membranes.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> positive immunohistochemical staining for AFP, GPC3, or SALL4.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138740,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant&nbsp;/ not described for orbital YSTs</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138741,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 178,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Prognostic and management guidelines are not available for primary orbital YST. Proptosis allowing early tumour detection may result in a better prognosis for orbital YST than other extragonadal YSTs {6677841}. Chemotherapy and radiotherapy may provide long-term disease-free survival {6677841;18835732}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:03:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]